{"headers":{"Accept-Encoding":"gzip, br","Cdn-Loop":"cloudflare; loops=1","Cf-Connecting-Ip":"163.176.73.79","Cf-Ipcountry":"BR","Cf-Ray":"a48a3c28fd53c98a-GRU","Cf-Visitor":"{\"scheme\":\"https\"}","Cf-Warp-Tag-Id":"27d7610a-bb9e-40bc-b3bf-8e95444838f6","Connection":"keep-alive","Content-Length":"17777","Content-Type":"application/json","User-Agent":"Go-http-client/1.1","X-Forgejo-Delivery":"c9999dc9-1b3f-4644-969f-ff0dac4d0d92","X-Forgejo-Event":"pull_request","X-Forgejo-Event-Type":"pull_request_sync","X-Forwarded-For":"163.176.73.79","X-Forwarded-Proto":"https","X-Gitea-Delivery":"c9999dc9-1b3f-4644-969f-ff0dac4d0d92","X-Gitea-Event":"pull_request","X-Gitea-Event-Type":"pull_request_sync","X-Github-Delivery":"c9999dc9-1b3f-4644-969f-ff0dac4d0d92","X-Github-Event":"pull_request","X-Github-Event-Type":"pull_request_sync","X-Gogs-Delivery":"c9999dc9-1b3f-4644-969f-ff0dac4d0d92","X-Gogs-Event":"pull_request","X-Gogs-Event-Type":"pull_request_sync"},"body":{"action":"synchronized","number":8,"pull_request":{"id":1455,"url":"https://git.terrascale.tech/api/v1/repos/TerraScale/ts-cos/pulls/8","number":8,"user":{"id":1,"login":"mariogk","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"","email":"admin@git.mariogk.com","avatar_url":"https://git.terrascale.tech/avatars/ed81dd55dce7cad54cda88d4af264be7","html_url":"https://git.terrascale.tech/mariogk","language":"en-US","is_admin":true,"last_login":"2026-09-21T22:46:05Z","created":"2026-04-08T23:53:08Z","restricted":false,"active":true,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":0,"username":"mariogk"},"title":"TS-811: Replicated COS chat page and shared context store","body":"Part of TS-811\n\nSlice 1 of 3: the dashboard home is now one chat with COS, replicated on every node.\n\n## What changed\n- `GET /` is the chat page: message list, composer (Ctrl/Cmd+Enter sends), markdown replies (goldmark, raw HTML and `javascript:` links dropped), collapsed \"N tool calls\", streaming marker, phone layout (`100dvh`, safe-area composer).\n- Header: running threads, PRs waiting, a Settings link, and empty slots `#heartbeat-slot` (TS-813) and `#inbox-slot` (TS-815).\n- Chat entries live in the replicated JetStream KV bucket `COS_CHAT`. Every node follows it in memory and pushes Datastar SSE patches: new entries append, edited entries morph in place, deleted entries are removed. The SSE stream reconnects without a retry limit.\n- `POST /chat` stores a user message. It requires the `Datastar-Request` header, so a basic-auth browser can't be driven cross-site.\n- Shared context files: `cos context list|get|set|rm` on the replicated KV bucket `COS_CONTEXT` (16 KiB per file).\n- Only the JetStream meta leader creates buckets. When nodes created the same R3 bucket at once, the stream assignment wedged and every create timed out; the other nodes now bind once the bucket exists.\n- Deleted the old read-only dashboard (`dashboard.templ`, `/events`) and its helpers (greenfield). `/status` JSON stays.\n\nNext slices: (2) the COS agent runtime on the leader (one T3 thread, brief, restarts, compaction, failover), (3) the COS queue (batching, debounce, digest, wake budget, tokens per wake).\n\n## Checks\n`nice -n 19 go tool templ generate && go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test ./...`: green. New tests cover 3-node replication, apply/order/cap, SSE append/morph/remove, header updates from SQLite changes, route guards, markdown safety and the context CLI.\n\n## Live check\nRun on an isolated 3-host cluster built from this branch rebased on main (main's `startBus` with a test master secret on ports 24811/26811, dashboard on 28811, test HOME `/tmp/cos-ts811`; the production `cos.service` was busy with TS-818 canary installs, so I stayed off it).\n1. All 3 nodes joined over Tailscale; `cos cluster` on each showed the same leader.\n2. `POST /chat` on beta \u2192 the SSE stream on mariogk-dev showed the message.\n3. `cos context set live-check ...` on mariogk-dev \u2192 `cos context get live-check` on delta returned it.\n4. Stopped beta, posted on delta, started beta \u2192 beta's stream showed both messages (catch-up from JetStream, no manual step).\n5. Before the rebase, the same checks passed on the old nats.conf build, plus a message typed in a Pixel 7-sized browser on beta that appeared on mariogk-dev.\n\n## Review fixes\n- A deleted or recreated chat bucket no longer freezes a node: each node checks the bucket's stream identity every 5 s and rebinds from a fresh replay (tested by deleting the bucket in the 3-node test).\n- Link and image destinations use an allowlist (http(s), mailto, `#`, `/`, relative); `JavaScript:`/`DATA:` mixed-case schemes are dropped (tests added).\n- The context key lister is stopped on every return path.\n- Rebased on TS-810/813/814. The old dashboard (and its TS-813 autopilot panel) is gone, so `/settings` now hosts the autopilot panel and the header slot shows the heartbeat interval and next beat. Also adapted `events_test.go`/`autopilot_test.go` to main's `startBus` test API (main's own test build was broken; #12 fixes the same).","labels":[],"milestone":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":null,"requested_reviewers":[{"id":3,"login":"terrascale-bot","login_name":"","source_id":0,"full_name":"TerraScale Deployment Bot","email":"terrascale-bot@noreply.git.terrascale.tech","avatar_url":"https://git.terrascale.tech/avatars/ccb6b331ff35ce5bc3dee5416ba0a9e8","html_url":"https://git.terrascale.tech/terrascale-bot","language":"","is_admin":false,"last_login":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","created":"2026-04-29T21:54:04Z","restricted":false,"active":false,"prohibit_login":false,"location":"","pronouns":"","website":"","description":"","visibility":"public","followers_count":0,"following_count":0,"starred_repos_count":0,"username":"terrascale-bot"}],"requested_reviewers_teams":[],"state":"open","draft":false,"is_locked":false,"comments":3,"re